-- title:
--   Closed Cutoff Energy Claim at Constant $153$
-- statement:
--   This is the closed finite-horizon cutoff form of the Bizeul–Klartag–Lehec estimate (95).
--
--   For every $d\in\mathbb N$ with $1\le d$, the cutoff energy proposition holds at parameter $153$:
--
--   $$
--   \operatorname{CutoffEnergyClaim}(153,d).
--   $$
--
--   This declaration is a technical intermediate estimate for every order $d+1\ge2$ and is used to produce the explicit cumulant bound with constant $153$.
--
--   **Formalization Note**: `CutoffEnergyClaim` is the repository's finite-horizon cutoff predicate; its internal analytic content is not expanded by the declaration type.
